{"type":"text","timestamp":1788168033502,"sessionID":"ses_fa8e24490ffe6DSQasHP6TF9R8","part":{"id":"prt_0571ed028001PxLmHN8gmk5TM1","messageID":"msg_0571ec5100013hkvkZL1u5aVw1","sessionID":"ses_fa8e24490ffe6DSQasHP6TF9R8","type":"text","text":"Production checks now pass: compilation succeeds, and manual integration checks cover both `Money` products, legacy `price_cents` dictionaries, reporting aggregation, and currency handling. The requested pytest command cannot execute here because neither `python` nor the `pytest` module is installed; I’m recording that limitation and the successful checks in the report.","time":{"start":1788168032296,"end":1788168033491},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_070f71aa0f0d29d1016a95476038a487d2b45b6d8be4e7d0f5","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788168039759,"sessionID":"ses_fa8e24490ffe6DSQasHP6TF9R8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_n0RisQidlYMU5EO4Tjoo94q0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n+# Interface Fix Report\n+\n+## Root Cause\n+\n+`catalog.Product` now exposes `price` as a `Money` object containing\n+`amount_cents` and `currency`. The orders adapter still read the removed\n+`price_cents` and top-level `currency` attributes, so orders using current\n+catalog products failed before reports could aggregate them.\n+\n+## Changes\n+\n+- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n+  - Reads `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` from current products.\n+  - Retains support for legacy dictionaries containing `price_cents` and\n+    `currency`.\n+- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`\n+  - Keeps currency validation and reports both currencies in the mixed-currency\n+    error message.\n+\n+The `Money` model and the reports output contract were preserved. No fixture\n+values or third-party dependencies were added.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+Requested command:\n+\n+```text\n+python -m pytest tests\n+```\n+\n+It could not run in this environment because `python` is unavailable and\n+`python3` has no installed `pytest` module.\n+\n+Successful checks:\n+\n+- `python3 -m compileall -q packages`\n+- Manual checks for current `Money` products, legacy `price_cents` dictionaries,\n+  report aggregation, and mixed-currency rejection.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n+++ /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@\n+# Interface Fix Report\n+\n+## Root Cause\n+\n+`catalog.Product` now exposes `price` as a `Money` object containing\n+`amount_cents` and `currency`. The orders adapter still read the removed\n+`price_cents` and top-level `currency` attributes, so orders using current\n+catalog products failed before reports could aggregate them.\n+\n+## Changes\n+\n+- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n+  - Reads `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` from current products.\n+  - Retains support for legacy dictionaries containing `price_cents` and\n+    `currency`.\n+- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`\n+  - Keeps currency validation and reports both currencies in the mixed-currency\n+    error message.\n+\n+The `Money` model and the reports output contract were preserved. No fixture\n+values or third-party dependencies were added.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+Requested command:\n+\n+```text\n+python -m pytest tests\n+```\n+\n+It could not run in this environment because `python` is unavailable and\n+`python3` has no installed `pytest` module.\n+\n+Successful checks:\n+\n+- `python3 -m compileall -q packages`\n+- Manual checks for current `Money` products, legacy `price_cents` dictionaries,\n+  report aggregation, and mixed-currency rejection.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","relativePath":"workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n+++ /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@\n+# Interface Fix Report\n+\n+## Root Cause\n+\n+`catalog.Product` now exposes `price` as a `Money` object containing\n+`amount_cents` and `currency`. The orders adapter still read the removed\n+`price_cents` and top-level `currency` attributes, so orders using current\n+catalog products failed before reports could aggregate them.\n+\n+## Changes\n+\n+- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n+  - Reads `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` from current products.\n+  - Retains support for legacy dictionaries containing `price_cents` and\n+    `currency`.\n+- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`\n+  - Keeps currency validation and reports both currencies in the mixed-currency\n+    error message.\n+\n+The `Money` model and the reports output contract were preserved. No fixture\n+values or third-party dependencies were added.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+Requested command:\n+\n+```text\n+python -m pytest tests\n+```\n+\n+It could not run in this environment because `python` is unavailable and\n+`python3` has no installed `pytest` module.\n+\n+Successful checks:\n+\n+- `python3 -m compileall -q packages`\n+- Manual checks for current `Money` products, legacy `price_cents` dictionaries,\n+  report aggregation, and mixed-currency rejection.\n","additions":38,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","time":{"start":1788168039754,"end":1788168039758}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_070f71aa0f0d29d1016a9547616e6887d2ad42d9f564a5dac4"}},"id":"prt_0571ed4da001941zwRKYz7OmaV","sessionID":"ses_fa8e24490ffe6DSQasHP6TF9R8","messageID":"msg_0571ec5100013hkvkZL1u5aVw1"}}
