{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788168046152,"sessionID":"ses_fa8e24490ffe6DSQasHP6TF9R8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_NmbUvFpYqpfBklLQBp3m1Fmc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Interface Fix Report\n2: \n3: ## Root Cause\n4: \n5: `catalog.Product` now exposes `price` as a `Money` object containing\n6: `amount_cents` and `currency`. The orders adapter still read the removed\n7: `price_cents` and top-level `currency` attributes, so orders using current\n8: catalog products failed before reports could aggregate them.\n9: \n10: ## Changes\n11: \n12: - `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n13:   - Reads `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` from current products.\n14:   - Retains support for legacy dictionaries containing `price_cents` and\n15:     `currency`.\n16: - `packages/orders/orders/service.py`\n17:   - Keeps currency validation and reports both currencies in the mixed-currency\n18:     error message.\n19: \n20: The `Money` model and the reports output contract were preserved. No fixture\n21: values or third-party dependencies were added.\n22: \n23: ## Verification\n24: \n25: Requested command:\n26: \n27: ```text\n28: python -m pytest tests\n29: ```\n30: \n31: It could not run in this environment because `python` is unavailable and\n32: `python3` has no installed `pytest` module.\n33: \n34: Successful checks:\n35: \n36: - `python3 -m compileall -q packages`\n37: - Manual checks for current `Money` products, legacy `price_cents` dictionaries,\n38:   report aggregation, and mixed-currency rejection.\n\n(End of file - total 38 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Interface Fix Report\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`catalog.Product` now exposes `price` as a `Money` object containing\n`amount_cents` and `currency`. The orders adapter still read the removed\n`price_cents` and top-level `currency` attributes, so orders using current\ncatalog products failed before reports could aggregate them.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n  - Reads `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` from current products.\n  - Retains support for legacy dictionaries containing `price_cents` and\n    `currency`.\n- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`\n  - Keeps currency validation and reports both currencies in the mixed-currency\n    error message.\n\nThe `Money` model and the reports output contract were preserved. No fixture","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","text":"# Interface Fix Report\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`catalog.Product` now exposes `price` as a `Money` object containing\n`amount_cents` and `currency`. The orders adapter still read the removed\n`price_cents` and top-level `currency` attributes, so orders using current\ncatalog products failed before reports could aggregate them.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n  - Reads `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` from current products.\n  - Retains support for legacy dictionaries containing `price_cents` and\n    `currency`.\n- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`\n  - Keeps currency validation and reports both currencies in the mixed-currency\n    error message.\n\nThe `Money` model and the reports output contract were preserved. No fixture\nvalues or third-party dependencies were added.\n\n## Verification\n\nRequested command:\n\n```text\npython -m pytest tests\n```\n\nIt could not run in this environment because `python` is unavailable and\n`python3` has no installed `pytest` module.\n\nSuccessful checks:\n\n- `python3 -m compileall -q packages`\n- Manual checks for current `Money` products, legacy `price_cents` dictionaries,\n  report aggregation, and mixed-currency rejection.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":38,"totalLines":38,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","time":{"start":1